# Trivy vulnerability exemptions — baseline §13.1 permits named exemptions but forbids
# silently ignoring Critical/High without one. Each line is one vulnerability identifier
# (CVE-XXXX-XXXX or VULNID). An entry MUST be accompanied by a `# <reason>` comment
# naming the SLA window (§13.3) and the remediation plan.
#
# Format (one per line):
#   CVE-2024-12345  # tracked in <issue>; deferred until <upstream fix> per §13.3 <SLA>
#
# This file is consumed by .github/workflows/sbom-and-scan.yml (Critical/High gate).
# The SARIF step still reports the full severity range so exemptions are visible.
